From 702b3740b68c5544a277cfccf49c535b45c216dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E7=94=B0=E5=AE=81?=
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 21:56:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: Add RVV wcschr with multiarch wiring
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add an e32 RVV wcschr kernel with an immediate-element fast path and a
four-way-unrolled scalar short-string window.  Probe the first vector
chunk with LMUL=1, then switch to an LMUL=8 page-aware long path which
uses ordinary loads inside a page and fault-only-first loads at page
boundaries.  Wire the vector and generic implementations into the
RISC-V multiarch IFUNC machinery.

Performance was measured on a SpacemiT K3 X100 core with VLEN=256,
pinned to CPU 2.  The userspace governor held the observed frequency at
2.2 GHz.  Baseline glibc commit:
afc3228df04b64d94519bd00b61907560208bbb1.

Commands:
    make test t=wcsmbs/test-wcschr
    BENCH_DURATION=3 USE_CLOCK_GETTIME=1 nice -n -20 taskset -c 2 \
        ./testrun.sh ./benchtests/bench-wcschr

One warmup and six formal runs were performed.  Baseline and vector were
measured as paired IFUNCs in every run.  Values below first take the
median of the six timings for each case and then the geometric mean;
lower is better.  Change is (baseline / vector - 1) * 100.

Metric                  Baseline  Patched  Change
All 498 cases            97.3628  38.8899  +150.36%
Position 0-7             12.0290   6.6355   +81.28%
Position 8-15            23.4753  15.0361   +56.13%
Position 16-31           35.7897  21.1917   +68.89%
Position >=32           228.6339  71.1581  +221.30%

Worst individual case (point median):

Metric                  Baseline  Patched  Change
Length 16, position 15   27.2750  22.4280   +21.61%

Its remaining parameters are rand=1, branch=1, perc-zero=1, and
alignment=0.  Unlike the preceding rows, this row represents one case
rather than a geometric mean over a group.

The vector implementation was faster in all 498 point-median cases.
The worst case still improved by 21.61%; no repeatable regression of 5%
or more was found.  The two immediate-NUL cases improved by 58.82% and
49.95%, while the two target-at-position-31 cases improved by 39.60% and
24.49%.

Validation:
- Incremental RISC-V build: PASS
- make test t=wcsmbs/test-wcschr: PASS
- Target benchmark coverage: 498/498 cases

Signed-off-by: 田宁
